const DESK={basics:["Basics desk","🌱","#10b981"],ratios:["Ratios desk","🧮","#6366f1"],reports:["Reports desk","📑","#0ea5e9"],risk:["Risk desk","🚩","#f43f5e"],money:["Money desk","💸","#f59e0b"]};
const POSTS=[
{id:"p1",t:"term",d:"basics",l:"Beginner",title:"Working capital",body:"Working capital = current assets − current liabilities. It shows whether a company can pay its short-term bills. Negative isn’t always bad (some retailers run on supplier credit), so always read it in context.",more:"chat/mentor/What is working capital?"},
{id:"p2",t:"fact",d:"money",l:"Beginner",title:"The Rule of 72",body:"Divide 72 by an annual return to estimate how many years it takes to double money. At 8% a year, 72 ÷ 8 ≈ 9 years. It’s a quick estimate, not a promise.",more:"chat/mentor/Explain compounding"},
{id:"p3",t:"myth",d:"reports",l:"Beginner",myth:"A profitable company always has plenty of cash.",fact:"Profit is an accounting figure. Cash flow shows the cash that actually came in. Compare net profit with operating cash flow.",more:"reels/ocf"},
{id:"p4",t:"term",d:"ratios",l:"Beginner",title:"Current ratio",body:"Current ratio = current assets ÷ current liabilities. Above 1 means short-term assets cover short-term obligations. What counts as healthy varies by industry.",more:"chat/mentor/What is the current ratio?"},
{id:"p5",t:"quiz",d:"ratios",l:"Beginner",q:"Debt doubles while equity stays the same. What happens to Debt-to-Equity?",opts:["It halves","It doubles","It stays the same"],ans:1,why:"D/E = Total debt ÷ Equity, so doubling debt doubles D/E.",more:"reels/de"},
{id:"p6",t:"list",d:"reports",l:"Beginner",title:"Five places to look in an annual report",items:["Balance sheet: equity and debt","Profit and loss: revenue and net profit","Cash flow statement: cash from operations","Notes to accounts: the details behind the numbers","Auditor’s report: any qualifications or concerns"],more:"reels/read"},
{id:"p7",t:"case",d:"ratios",l:"Intermediate",setup:"Fictional case: Zeta Ltd has an ROE of 24%, but its Debt-to-Equity is 2.6. Is it a star performer?",reveal:"Not necessarily. High ROE can come from heavy borrowing. Check leverage and interest cover before drawing conclusions.",more:"reels/roe"},
{id:"p8",t:"term",d:"ratios",l:"Advanced",title:"DuPont analysis",body:"ROE = Net profit margin × Asset turnover × Equity multiplier. It splits ROE into profitability, efficiency and leverage, so you can see why ROE is high or low.",more:"chat/mentor/Explain DuPont analysis"},
{id:"p9",t:"fact",d:"money",l:"Beginner",title:"Compounding in action",body:"₹10,000 growing at 10% a year becomes about ₹25,937 after 10 years. The longer the time, the bigger the effect. Returns are never guaranteed.",more:"chat/mentor/Explain compounding"},
{id:"p10",t:"myth",d:"basics",l:"Intermediate",myth:"A low P/E ratio always means a stock is cheap.",fact:"P/E compares price with earnings. A low P/E can reflect weak growth or higher risk. Compare companies within the same industry.",more:"chat/mentor/What is the P/E ratio?"},
{id:"p11",t:"term",d:"reports",l:"Intermediate",title:"Free cash flow",body:"Free cash flow = operating cash flow − capital expenditure. It’s the cash left after the business invests in its assets. Consistently positive free cash flow is a healthy sign.",more:"chat/mentor/What is free cash flow?"},
{id:"p12",t:"poll",d:"reports",l:"Beginner",q:"Where would you look first in an annual report?",opts:["Revenue trend","Debt level","Cash flow","Auditor’s notes"],why:"There’s no single right answer. Many analysts start with the revenue trend, then check debt and cash flow, and finally read the auditor’s notes.",more:"reels/read"},
{id:"p13",t:"term",d:"risk",l:"Intermediate",title:"Interest coverage",body:"Interest coverage = operating profit (EBIT) ÷ interest expense. It shows how comfortably a company can pay its interest. Low values (for example below about 1.5) can be a warning sign, though rules of thumb vary.",more:"chat/mentor/What is interest coverage?"},
{id:"p14",t:"fact",d:"money",l:"Beginner",title:"Inflation eats savings",body:"If inflation is 6% and your savings earn 4%, your real return is about −2% before tax. Always compare returns with inflation.",more:"chat/mentor/What is inflation?"},
{id:"p15",t:"quiz",d:"reports",l:"Beginner",q:"Operating cash flow comes mainly from…",opts:["Selling new shares","Core business activities","Taking a bank loan"],ans:1,why:"Operating cash flow is the cash generated by the core business. Share sales and loans appear under financing activities.",more:"reels/ocf"},
{id:"p16",t:"term",d:"basics",l:"Intermediate",title:"Book value",body:"Book value per share = shareholders’ equity ÷ number of shares. It’s an accounting measure of net worth per share, not the same as market price.",more:"chat/mentor/What is book value?"},
{id:"p17",t:"tip",d:"ratios",l:"Beginner",title:"Compare like with like",body:"Ratios mean different things in different industries. Compare a software company with software peers, and a bank with banks. Comparing across industries can mislead.",more:"chat/mentor/How do I compare companies?"},
{id:"p18",t:"term",d:"reports",l:"Advanced",title:"EBITDA",body:"EBITDA = earnings before interest, tax, depreciation and amortisation. It’s a proxy for operating performance, but it ignores capital spending and debt costs, so don’t use it alone.",more:"chat/mentor/What is EBITDA?"},
{id:"p19",t:"myth",d:"money",l:"Intermediate",myth:"If a company pays dividends, it must be financially healthy.",fact:"Dividends can be paid from reserves or even borrowing. Check that operating cash flow comfortably supports them.",more:"chat/mentor/What is a dividend?"},
{id:"p20",t:"fact",d:"reports",l:"Intermediate",title:"The three statements are linked",body:"Net profit from the profit and loss flows into the balance sheet through retained earnings, and the cash flow statement explains how profit turned into cash. If they don’t tell a consistent story, dig deeper.",more:"reels/score"},
{id:"p21",t:"case",d:"risk",l:"Intermediate",setup:"Fictional case: Delta Ltd’s profit rose 30%, but its operating cash flow fell 20%. Good news?",reveal:"Be careful. Profit may be stuck in receivables or inventory instead of becoming cash. Check working capital changes.",more:"reels/ocf"},
{id:"p22",t:"list",d:"risk",l:"Intermediate",title:"Red flags to look for",items:["Receivables growing much faster than revenue","Profit rising while operating cash flow falls","Frequent changes in auditors or accounting policies","Large related-party transactions","Heavy borrowing to fund day-to-day operations"],more:"reels/flags"},
{id:"p23",t:"fact",d:"money",l:"Beginner",title:"What a SIP does",body:"A Systematic Investment Plan invests a fixed amount at regular intervals. You buy more units when prices are low and fewer when they’re high. It builds discipline but doesn’t guarantee profit.",more:"chat/mentor/What is a SIP?"},
{id:"p24",t:"term",d:"risk",l:"Intermediate",title:"Pledged shares",body:"When promoters pledge their shares as collateral for loans, a sharp price fall can force sales. High pledging is a risk factor worth checking in the shareholding pattern.",more:"chat/mentor/What are pledged shares?"},
{id:"p25",t:"quiz",d:"ratios",l:"Intermediate",q:"Net profit rises while equity stays the same. ROE…",opts:["Falls","Rises","Stays the same"],ans:1,why:"ROE = Net profit ÷ Equity, so higher profit with the same equity means a higher ROE.",more:"reels/quiz"},
{id:"p26",t:"tip",d:"reports",l:"Intermediate",title:"Read the management discussion",body:"The Management Discussion & Analysis explains the year in the company’s own words: risks, outlook and segment performance. Compare its story with the numbers.",more:"reels/read"},
{id:"p27",t:"term",d:"basics",l:"Beginner",title:"Leverage",body:"Leverage means using borrowed money to try to boost returns. It can raise ROE in good years and magnify losses in bad ones.",more:"reels/de"},
{id:"p28",t:"poll",d:"basics",l:"Beginner",q:"What matters most for a long-term investor?",opts:["Past returns","Business quality","Daily price moves"],why:"Past returns don’t guarantee the future. Many long-term investors focus on business quality: stable earnings, manageable debt and healthy cash flow.",more:"reels/score"}];
const FST=()=>UJ("fs_feed",{likes:[],saves:[],cm:{},ans:{},mine:[]}),FSW=S=>UW("fs_feed",S);let FS={cat:"All",shown:0,order:[],obs:null};
const feedShell=()=>`<h2 style="margin-top:14px">FinFeed</h2><p class="mu" style="margin:-4px 0 8px;font-size:.88rem">Bite-sized finance: terms, myths, quizzes and cases.</p><div id="fchips" style="display:flex;gap:6px;overflow-x:auto;padding-bottom:6px">${["All","Beginner","Intermediate","Advanced","Saved"].map(c=>`<button class="ch ${FS.cat==c?"on":""}" data-fc="${c}">${c}</button>`).join("")}</div><div class="card"><b>Share a tip</b><textarea id="fpt" class="inp" rows="2" maxlength="280" placeholder="Teach something about finance in a few lines…" style="margin-top:6px"></textarea><div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:8px;margin-top:8px"><small>Educational only. No buy/sell calls. Visible on this device.</small><button class="btn bl" data-fa="post" style="width:auto;margin:0;padding:9px 18px">Post</button></div></div><div id="feed"></div><div id="fmore" class="mu" style="text-align:center;padding:16px"></div>`;
function feedOrder(){const S=FST(),r=seeded(dayN()*7919+1),P=[...POSTS];for(let i=P.length-1;i>0;i--){const j=Math.floor(r()*(i+1));[P[i],P[j]]=[P[j],P[i]]}let L=[...S.mine,...P];if(FS.cat=="Saved")L=L.filter(x=>S.saves.includes(x.id));else if(FS.cat!="All")L=L.filter(x=>x.l==FS.cat);return L}
function markQuiz(po,P,i){const o=po.querySelectorAll(".qo");o.forEach((b,j)=>{if(j==P.ans)b.classList.add("ok");else if(j==i)b.classList.add("no")});const a=po.querySelector(".ans");a.hidden=false;a.textContent=(i==P.ans?"✅ Correct! ":"Not quite. ")+P.why}
function markPoll(po,P,i){const o=po.querySelectorAll(".qo");o.forEach((b,j)=>{if(j==i)b.classList.add("pk")});const a=po.querySelector(".ans");a.hidden=false;a.textContent="You chose “"+P.opts[i]+"”. "+P.why}
function postHTML(p){const S=FST(),dk=p.t=="user"?[p.n,"🧑‍🎓","#7c3aed"]:DESK[p.d],liked=S.likes.includes(p.id),sv=S.saves.includes(p.id),cm=S.cm[p.id]||[],an=S.ans[p.id];let b="";
const T={term:"Term",fact:"Did you know?",tip:"Tip"};
if(p.t=="term"||p.t=="fact"||p.t=="tip")b=`<span class="tg2">${T[p.t]}</span><h3>${ESC(p.title)}</h3><p>${ESC(p.body)}</p>`;
else if(p.t=="myth")b=`<span class="tg2 r">Myth</span><h3>“${ESC(p.myth)}”</h3><button class="rv" data-fa="reveal">Tap to reveal the fact</button><div class="ans" hidden><span class="tg2 g">Fact</span><p>${ESC(p.fact)}</p></div>`;
else if(p.t=="case")b=`<span class="tg2">Case</span><p style="margin-top:6px">${ESC(p.setup)}</p><button class="rv" data-fa="reveal">Reveal the catch</button><div class="ans" hidden><span class="tg2 g">The catch</span><p>${ESC(p.reveal)}</p></div>`;
else if(p.t=="quiz"||p.t=="poll"){const a=an!=null;b=`<span class="tg2">${p.t=="quiz"?"Quiz":"Poll"}</span><h3>${ESC(p.q)}</h3>${p.opts.map((o,i)=>`<button class="qo ${a?(p.t=="quiz"?(i==p.ans?"ok":i==an?"no":""):(i==an?"pk":"")):""}" data-fa="${p.t=="quiz"?"opt":"vote"}" data-i="${i}">${ESC(o)}</button>`).join("")}<div class="ans" ${a?"":"hidden"}>${a?(p.t=="quiz"?(an==p.ans?"✅ Correct! ":"Not quite. ")+ESC(p.why):"You chose “"+ESC(p.opts[an])+"”. "+ESC(p.why)):""}</div>`}
else if(p.t=="list")b=`<span class="tg2">Checklist</span><h3>${ESC(p.title)}</h3><ul>${p.items.map(x=>`<li>${ESC(x)}</li>`).join("")}</ul>`;
else b=`<p style="margin-top:0">${ESC(p.body)}</p>`;
return`<article class="po" data-id="${p.id}"><div class="ph2"><div class="pav" style="background:${dk[2]}">${dk[1]}</div><div class="pn"><b>${ESC(dk[0])}</b><small style="display:block">${p.t=="user"?"Community tip · only on this device":"FinScore Academy ✔"}</small></div><span class="lvl">${p.l||"Community"}</span></div><div class="pbd">${b}</div><div class="pa2"><button data-fa="like" class="${liked?"on":""}" aria-label="Like">${liked?"❤️":"🤍"}</button><button data-fa="cm" aria-label="Comments">💬 ${cm.length||""}</button><button data-fa="save" class="${sv?"on":""}" aria-label="Save">🔖</button><button data-fa="share" aria-label="Share">↗</button>${p.more?`<a class="lm" href="#/${p.more}">Learn more ›</a>`:""}</div><div class="pcm" hidden><div class="cl">${cm.map(c=>`<p><b>${ESC(c.n)}</b> ${ESC(c.t)}</p>`).join("")}</div><div class="cin"><input placeholder="Add a comment…" maxlength="160" aria-label="Comment"><button data-fa="send">Send</button></div></div></article>`}
function moreFeed(){const f=$("#feed"),m=$("#fmore");if(!f||!m)return;if(!FS.order.length){m.textContent=FS.cat=="Saved"?"Nothing saved yet. Tap 🔖 on a post to keep it here.":"No posts here yet.";return}const n=FS.order.slice(FS.shown,FS.shown+4);n.forEach(p=>f.insertAdjacentHTML("beforeend",postHTML(p)));FS.shown+=n.length;const more=FS.shown<FS.order.length;m.textContent=more?"Loading more…":"You’re all caught up. New posts every day.";if(!more&&FS.obs)FS.obs.unobserve(m);else if(FS.obs){FS.obs.unobserve(m);FS.obs.observe(m)}}
function feedInit(){dailyTip();FS.order=feedOrder();FS.shown=0;const f=$("#feed");if(!f)return;f.innerHTML="";FS.obs=new IntersectionObserver(e=>{if(e[0].isIntersecting)moreFeed()},{root:$("#scr"),rootMargin:"300px"});moreFeed();FS.obs.observe($("#fmore"))}
function feedStop(){if(FS.obs){FS.obs.disconnect();FS.obs=null}}
/* FinChat + FinMentor */
const CH={mentor:{n:"FinMentor",e:"🤖",sub:"Bot · ask anything about finance",bot:true},general:{n:"#general",e:"💬",sub:"Public channel · preview"},ratios:{n:"#ratios-help",e:"🧮",sub:"Public channel · preview"},exam:{n:"#exam-prep",e:"🎓",sub:"Public channel · preview"}};
const SEED={general:[["Aarav","Anyone else finding the cash flow statement tricky?"],["Meera","Start with operating, investing, financing. Operating cash flow matters most for the score."]],ratios:[["Kabir","Why is ROE high but D/E also high for the same company?"],["Sana","Leverage can boost ROE. Check the DuPont split!"]],exam:[["Ishaan","Which formulas should I remember for the viva?"],["Riya","ROE, D/E and revenue growth. Practise with the sample PDFs."]]};
const CHN=()=>UJ("fs_chat",{});
const KB=[{id:"adv",k:[],a:"I can’t give buy, sell or hold advice or stock tips. FinScore is an analysis aid. I can explain ratios and how to read a report, and a qualified adviser can help with investment decisions."},
{k:["roe","return on equity"],a:"ROE (Return on Equity) = Net profit ÷ Shareholders’ equity. It shows how much profit a company earns on the owners’ money. For example, 17% means ₹17 profit for every ₹100 of equity. In FinScore, a higher ROE scores higher (subject to validation)."},
{k:["debt","d/e","leverage","borrow"],a:"Debt-to-Equity (D/E) = Total debt ÷ Shareholders’ equity. A D/E of 0.8 means ₹80 of debt for every ₹100 of owners’ money. FinScore gives higher scores to lower leverage, but what’s healthy varies by industry."},
{k:["cash flow","ocf","operating cash"],a:"Operating cash flow is the cash a company generates from its core business. Profit can look good on paper while cash is stuck in receivables or inventory, so FinScore checks cash flow too. Positive operating cash flow adds to the score."},
{k:["revenue growth","sales growth","growth"],a:"Revenue growth = [(Current revenue − Previous revenue) ÷ Previous revenue] × 100. Positive growth adds to the FinScore."},
{k:["score","finscore","calculated","calculate"],a:"FinScore uses four ratios: ROE, Debt-to-Equity, operating cash flow and revenue growth. Each gets a rule-based score from 0 to 100, and the overall score is the average of the valid ones. Missing or flagged metrics are left out. It’s an analysis aid, not advice."},
{k:["working capital"],a:"Working capital = current assets − current liabilities. It shows whether a company can meet its short-term obligations."},
{k:["current ratio"],a:"Current ratio = current assets ÷ current liabilities. Above 1 means short-term assets cover short-term obligations; healthy levels vary by industry."},
{k:["ebitda"],a:"EBITDA = earnings before interest, tax, depreciation and amortisation. It approximates operating performance but ignores capital spending and debt costs."},
{k:["p/e","pe ratio","price to earnings","price-to-earnings"],a:"P/E = share price ÷ earnings per share. It shows what the market pays for each ₹1 of earnings. A low P/E isn’t automatically cheap; compare within the same industry."},
{k:["free cash flow","fcf"],a:"Free cash flow = operating cash flow − capital expenditure. It’s the cash left after investing in the business."},
{k:["interest coverage"],a:"Interest coverage = EBIT ÷ interest expense. It shows how comfortably a company can pay its interest. Very low values can be a warning sign."},
{k:["dupont"],a:"DuPont analysis: ROE = Net profit margin × Asset turnover × Equity multiplier. It shows whether ROE comes from profitability, efficiency or leverage."},
{k:["book value"],a:"Book value per share = Shareholders’ equity ÷ Number of shares. It’s an accounting figure and differs from the market price."},
{k:["dividend"],a:"A dividend is a share of profit paid to shareholders. Check that operating cash flow supports it; a company can pay dividends from reserves or borrowing."},
{k:["compound","rule of 72"],a:"Compounding means earning returns on your earlier returns. ₹10,000 at 10% a year grows to about ₹25,937 in 10 years. The Rule of 72 estimates doubling time: 72 ÷ annual return."},
{k:["inflation"],a:"Inflation is the general rise in prices. If it’s 6% and your savings earn 4%, your real return is about −2% before tax."},
{k:["sip"],a:"A SIP (Systematic Investment Plan) invests a fixed amount regularly. It builds discipline and averages your purchase cost, but doesn’t guarantee profit."},
{k:["pledge"],a:"Pledged shares are shares promoters give as collateral for loans. High pledging can be risky if prices fall sharply."},
{k:["balance sheet"],a:"The balance sheet is a snapshot of assets, liabilities and equity on a date. FinScore reads shareholders’ equity and total borrowings from it."},
{k:["profit and loss","p&l","income statement"],a:"The statement of profit and loss shows revenue, expenses and net profit over a year. FinScore reads revenue and net profit from it."},
{k:["annual report","read a report","how to read","compare companies"],a:"Start with the balance sheet (equity, debt), the profit and loss (revenue, net profit) and the cash flow statement (operating cash flow). Then read the notes to accounts and the auditor’s report. Compare companies only within the same industry."},
{k:["missing","flagged","invalid","unavailable"],a:"If a required value is missing, FinScore marks that metric unavailable and leaves it out of the score. If a value looks invalid, it’s flagged and excluded. See the Limitations page for details."},
{k:["upload","pdf"],a:"Tap Upload, choose a text-based annual-report PDF and tap Analyze Report. FinScore reads equity, net profit, borrowings, operating cash flow and revenue for you. Try the sample PDFs to see how it works."},
{k:["who built","team","developed"],a:"FinScore PDF is developed by Team FinScore at Atharva College of Engineering."},
{k:["thank"],a:"You’re welcome! Ask me about any ratio or term anytime."},
{k:["hello","hi","hey","help"],a:"Hi! I’m FinMentor 🤖. Ask me about ROE, debt, cash flow, growth, how the score works, or tap “Explain my report”."}];
function myReportAnswer(){const r=mine[0];if(!r)return"You haven’t analysed a report yet. Tap Upload, choose an annual-report PDF, and I’ll explain the result.";const c=calc(r),L=c.M.map(m=>`• ${m.n}: ${m.disp} (${m.status}${m.score!=null&&m.status=="Valid"?", score "+m.score+"/100":""})`).join("\n"),v=c.M.filter(m=>m.status=="Valid"&&m.score!=null).sort((a,b)=>b.score-a.score);return`${r.name}, Annual Report ${r.year}: FinScore ${c.score}/100 (${c.label}).\n${L}`+(v.length>1?`\nStrongest: ${v[0].n}. Weakest: ${v[v.length-1].n}.`:"")+"\nThis is an analysis aid, not advice."}
function mentorAnswer(t){const x=t.toLowerCase();if(/\b(buy|sell|hold|target price|multibagger|which stock|should i invest|recommend)\b/.test(x))return KB[0].a;if(/(my|the) (report|score|result|analysis)|explain my/.test(x))return myReportAnswer();
let best=null,bs=0;KB.slice(1).forEach(e=>{let s=0;e.k.forEach(k=>{const re=new RegExp("\\b"+k.replace(/[.*+?^${}()|[\]\\\/]/g,"\\$&")+(k.length<=3?"\\b":""));if(re.test(x))s+=k.length});if(s>bs){bs=s;best=e}});
return best?best.a:"I’m not sure about that yet. Try asking about ROE, debt, cash flow, revenue growth, working capital, EBITDA, P/E, or tap “Explain my report”."}
function chatMsgs(id){const C=CHN();if(C[id])return C[id];const c=CH[id];if(c.bot)return[{u:"bot",t:"Hi! I’m FinMentor 🤖. Ask me about ROE, debt, cash flow, growth, or how your score works, or tap “Explain my report”. I can’t give buy or sell advice.",ts:Date.now()}];return(SEED[id]||[]).map(m=>({u:m[0],t:m[1],ts:0,seed:1}))}
const bubble=m=>m.u=="me"?`<div class="bb me">${ESC(m.t)}</div>`:`<div class="bb ot"><small>${m.u=="bot"?"FinMentor (bot)":ESC(m.u)+(m.seed?" · sample":"")}</small>${ESC(m.t)}</div>`;
const scrollChat=()=>{const s=$("#scr");if(s)s.scrollTop=s.scrollHeight};
function sendMsg(id,text){text=(text||"").trim();const c=CH[id];if(!text||!c)return;if(!c.bot&&!okText(text)){toast(BAD);return}const C=CHN(),L=C[id]||chatMsgs(id);L.push({u:"me",t:text,ts:Date.now()});C[id]=L;UW("fs_chat",C);const box=$("#msgs");if(box)box.insertAdjacentHTML("beforeend",bubble(L[L.length-1]));scrollChat();
if(c.bot||/\?|@mentor/i.test(text)){const tp=document.createElement("div");tp.className="bb ot";tp.innerHTML="<small>FinMentor (bot)</small>typing…";if(box)box.appendChild(tp);scrollChat();setTimeout(()=>{const r=mentorAnswer(text),C2=CHN(),L2=C2[id]||L;L2.push({u:"bot",t:r,ts:Date.now()});C2[id]=L2;UW("fs_chat",C2);if(tp.isConnected){tp.outerHTML=bubble({u:"bot",t:r});scrollChat()}},650)}}
function chatInit(id,q){scrollChat();const path=curPath();if(q&&CH[id]&&CH[id].bot&&window.__qa!=path){window.__qa=path;setTimeout(()=>sendMsg(id,decodeURIComponent(q)),350)}}
document.addEventListener("keydown",e=>{if(e.key!="Enter")return;if(e.target.id=="cin"){sendMsg(curPath().split("/")[1],e.target.value);e.target.value=""}else if(e.target.closest&&e.target.closest(".cin")){const b=e.target.closest(".cin").querySelector("button");if(b)b.click()}});
document.addEventListener("click",async e=>{const b=e.target.closest("[data-fa]"),fc=e.target.closest("[data-fc]"),nb=e.target.closest("#nbar");
if(nb){const h=nb.dataset.href;nb.hidden=true;if(h)nav(h);return}
if(fc){FS.cat=fc.dataset.fc;$("#fchips").querySelectorAll(".ch").forEach(x=>x.classList.toggle("on",x==fc));FS.order=feedOrder();FS.shown=0;$("#feed").innerHTML="";moreFeed();return}
if(!b)return;const a=b.dataset.fa,po=b.closest(".po"),id=po&&po.dataset.id,S=FST(),P=id&&[...S.mine,...POSTS].find(x=>x.id==id);
if(a=="send-msg"){const i=$("#cin");sendMsg(curPath().split("/")[1],i.value);i.value="";return}
if(a=="ask"){sendMsg(curPath().split("/")[1],b.dataset.q);return}
if(a=="invite"){const url=location.origin+location.pathname,text="Try FinScore PDF: understand annual reports with clarity.";try{if(navigator.share){await navigator.share({title:"FinScore PDF",text,url});return}}catch(x){if(x.name=="AbortError")return}try{await navigator.clipboard.writeText(text+" "+url);toast("Link copied")}catch(x){toast("Sharing isn’t available here")}return}
if(a=="post"){const t=$("#fpt").value.trim();if(t.length<10){toast("Write at least a short sentence");return}if(!okText(t)){toast(BAD);return}S.mine.unshift({id:"u"+Date.now(),t:"user",n:U.n,l:"Community",body:t});FSW(S);$("#fpt").value="";FS.order=feedOrder();FS.shown=0;$("#feed").innerHTML="";moreFeed();toast("Posted on this device");return}
if(!po||!P)return;
if(a=="like"||a=="save"){const k=a=="like"?"likes":"saves",n=S[k].indexOf(id);n>-1?S[k].splice(n,1):S[k].push(id);FSW(S);b.classList.toggle("on",n==-1);if(a=="like")b.textContent=n==-1?"❤️":"🤍";else toast(n==-1?"Saved to your notes":"Removed from saved");return}
if(a=="cm"){const c=po.querySelector(".pcm");c.hidden=!c.hidden;return}
if(a=="send"){const i=po.querySelector(".cin input"),t=i.value.trim();if(!t)return;if(!okText(t)){toast(BAD);return}(S.cm[id]=S.cm[id]||[]).push({n:U.n,t,ts:Date.now()});FSW(S);po.querySelector(".cl").insertAdjacentHTML("beforeend",`<p><b>${ESC(U.n)}</b> ${ESC(t)}</p>`);i.value="";po.querySelector("[data-fa=cm]").textContent="💬 "+S.cm[id].length;return}
if(a=="reveal"){po.querySelector(".ans").hidden=false;b.hidden=true;return}
if(a=="opt"||a=="vote"){if(S.ans[id]!=null)return;const i=+b.dataset.i;S.ans[id]=i;FSW(S);a=="opt"?markQuiz(po,P,i):markPoll(po,P,i);return}
if(a=="share"){const url=location.origin+location.pathname,text=(P.title||P.q||P.setup||P.myth||"A finance tip")+" — on FinScore PDF";try{if(navigator.share){await navigator.share({title:"FinScore PDF",text,url});return}}catch(x){if(x.name=="AbortError")return}try{await navigator.clipboard.writeText(text+" "+url);toast("Link copied")}catch(x){toast("Sharing isn’t available here")}}});

/* ===== v5: voice, dashboards, multi-company compare ===== */
const SMP=[{n:"TSC Ltd",v:[2400,408,1920,388,5200,5590]},{n:"Nova Pharma Ltd",v:[3100,620,900,710,4800,5600]},{n:"Zenith Steel Ltd",v:[1800,150,2700,90,7200,6900]},{n:"BlueWave Tech Ltd",v:[1500,390,200,420,2100,2900]}];
const VOX={roe:"ROE tells you how well a company turns the owners’ money into profit. If ROE is twenty percent, every hundred rupees of equity earned twenty rupees. Higher is usually better, but check debt too, because borrowing can inflate it.",de:"Debt to equity compares what the company owes with what the owners put in. A ratio of one means equal debt and equity. Lower usually means safer, though healthy levels depend on the industry.",ocf:"Operating cash flow is real cash from the core business. Profit can exist only on paper, so if cash stays well below profit, ask why.",growth:"Revenue growth shows whether sales are rising. Compare this year with last year, and remember that steady growth matters more than one big jump."};
let VC=null,spTok=0,CM=[],cmM=false,voiceOK=false,lastT="",wd=0;
const pickVoice=()=>{try{const sc=x=>(/en[-_]IN/i.test(x.lang)?30:15)+(/natural|neural|online/i.test(x.name)?25:0)+(/google|samantha|aria|jenny|zira|veena|neerja|heera|female/i.test(x.name)?12:0);return speechSynthesis.getVoices().filter(x=>/^en/i.test(x.lang)).sort((a,b)=>sc(b)-sc(a))[0]||null}catch(e){return null}};
if("speechSynthesis"in window)speechSynthesis.onvoiceschanged=()=>{VC=pickVoice()};
function setSpk(on){document.querySelectorAll(".reel.speaking").forEach(e=>e.classList.remove("speaking"));const el=on&&$(`.reel[data-i="${RS.i}"]`);if(el)el.classList.add("speaking")}
function speak(t,done,force){if(!("speechSynthesis"in window)||(!force&&!RS.sound))return false;try{const tok=++spTok;lastT=t;clearTimeout(wd);if(!voiceOK)wd=setTimeout(()=>{if(tok==spTok&&!voiceOK){showHint();try{speechSynthesis.cancel()}catch(e){}setSpk(false);done&&done()}},4500);speechSynthesis.cancel();try{speechSynthesis.resume()}catch(e){}VC=VC||pickVoice();const P=t.replace(/([.!?])\s+/g,"$1|").split("|").map(x=>x.trim()).filter(Boolean);let i=0;const nx=()=>{if(tok!=spTok)return;if(i>=P.length){setSpk(false);done&&done();return}const u=new SpeechSynthesisUtterance(P[i++]);if(VC){u.voice=VC;u.lang=VC.lang}else u.lang="en-IN";u.rate=.97;u.pitch=1.04;u.onstart=()=>{voiceOK=true;hideHint();setSpk(true)};u.onend=nx;u.onerror=()=>{if(tok==spTok){setSpk(false);done&&done()}};speechSynthesis.speak(u)};nx();return true}catch(e){return false}}
const vo=(L,c)=>{let t=sayText(c);if(c.t=="formula"&&VOX[L.id])t+=" "+VOX[L.id];if(!window.__hi){window.__hi=1;t="Hi, I’m Fin, your finance explainer. "+t}return t};
function showScene(){const L=RS.list[RS.i],el=L&&$(`.reel[data-i="${RS.i}"]`);if(!el)return;const c=L.scenes[RS.s],d=dur(c),snd=RS.sound&&"speechSynthesis"in window;el.classList.remove("paused");
el.querySelectorAll(".pbar span").forEach((sp,k)=>{sp.className=k<RS.s?"done":k==RS.s?(d&&!snd?"on":"on hold"):"";if(k==RS.s&&d)sp.style.setProperty("--d",d+"s")});
const st=el.querySelector(".stage");st.innerHTML=sceneHTML(c,L);st.querySelectorAll(".cu").forEach(countUp);const i0=RS.i,s0=RS.s;
if(snd){const vt=vo(L,c);showSub(el,vt);const ok=speak(vt,()=>{if(d&&RS.i==i0&&RS.s==s0)setTimeout(()=>{if(RS.i==i0&&RS.s==s0)rNext()},700)});if(!ok&&d)el.querySelectorAll(".pbar span")[RS.s].className="on"}else{showSub(el,"");setSpk(false);try{spTok++;speechSynthesis.cancel()}catch(e){}}}
document.addEventListener("click",e=>{const b=e.target.closest("[data-say]");if(!b||!("speechSynthesis"in window))return;if(speechSynthesis.speaking){spTok++;speechSynthesis.cancel();b.textContent="🔊 Listen";return}speak(b.dataset.say,()=>{b.textContent="🔊 Listen"},true);b.textContent="⏹ Stop"});
/* dashboards */
function gauge(s){const P=(p,r)=>{const a=Math.PI*(1-p/100);return(110+r*Math.cos(a)).toFixed(1)+","+(110-r*Math.sin(a)).toFixed(1)},A=(a,b,c)=>`<path d="M${P(a,80)} A80 80 0 0 1 ${P(b,80)}" fill="none" stroke="${c}" stroke-width="16"/>`;
return`<svg viewBox="0 0 220 135" width="260" role="img" aria-label="FinScore gauge ${s} out of 100">${A(0,55,"#f43f5e")}${A(55,80,"#f59e0b")}${A(80,100,"#10b981")}<g class="ndl" style="transform:rotate(${(-90+s*1.8).toFixed(1)}deg)"><line x1="110" y1="110" x2="110" y2="42" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="4" stroke-linecap="round"/></g><circle cx="110" cy="110" r="8" fill="currentColor"/><text x="110" y="132" text-anchor="middle" font-size="20" font-weight="800" fill="currentColor">${s}</text><text x="22" y="128" font-size="9" fill="currentColor">0</text><text x="190" y="128" font-size="9" fill="currentColor">100</text></svg>`}
function cols(it){const v=it.map(x=>Math.max(0,+x[1]||0)),mx=Math.max(...v,1),w=300/it.length;return`<svg viewBox="0 0 300 150" width="100%" role="img" aria-label="Column chart">${it.map((x,k)=>{const h=v[k]/mx*90,cx=k*w+w/2;return`<rect class="cb" x="${cx-16}" y="${115-h}" width="32" height="${h}" rx="4" fill="${x[2]}"/><text x="${cx}" y="${110-h}" text-anchor="middle" font-size="9" font-weight="700" fill="currentColor">${x[1]==null?"n/a":Math.round(x[1]).toLocaleString("en-IN")}</text><text x="${cx}" y="131" text-anchor="middle" font-size="9" fill="currentColor">${x[0]}</text>`}).join("")}<line x1="0" y1="115" x2="300" y2="115" stroke="var(--line)"/></svg>`}
function dash(r,c){const i=r.inp,v=c.M,ok=m=>m.status=="Valid"&&m.score!=null;
return`<h2 style="margin-top:18px">📊 Your dashboard</h2><div class="card dsh gz">${gauge(c.score)}<b style="display:block">${c.label}</b><button class="ch" style="margin:10px 0 0" data-say="${ESC(simple(r,c))}">🔊 Listen</button></div>
<div class="card dsh"><h3>Metric scores</h3>${v.map(m=>`<div class="br"><span>${m.n.replace("Operating Cash Flow","Cash flow").replace("Debt-to-Equity","D/E")}</span><div class="bt2"><i style="--w:${ok(m)?m.score:0}%;background:${MC[m.k]}"></i></div><b>${ok(m)?m.score:"n/a"}</b></div>`).join("")}</div>
<div class="card dsh"><h3>Score scale</h3>${v.filter(ok).map(m=>`<small>${m.n} · ${m.disp}</small><div class="sc2" style="--p:${m.score}%"><i><em>${m.score}</em></i></div><div class="scl"><span>Weak</span><span>Fair</span><span>Strong</span></div>`).join("")||'<p class="mu">No valid metrics to show.</p>'}</div>
<div class="card dsh"><h3>Key figures (₹ crore)</h3>${cols([["Equity",i.eq,"#6366f1"],["Debt",i.debt,"#14b8a6"],["Profit",i.np,"#f59e0b"],["Op. cash",i.ocf,"#ec4899"]])}</div>
<div class="card dsh"><h3>Revenue: last year vs this year</h3>${cols([["Previous",i.prev,"#818cf8"],["Current",i.cur,"#34d399"]])}</div>
<div class="card dsh" style="text-align:center"><h3>Strength radar</h3>${radar([{m:v.map(m=>ok(m)?m.score:0),c:"#6366f1"}])}</div>`}
const homeDash=()=>{const L=mine.slice(0,5);return`<div class="card dsh"><h2>📊 Your dashboard</h2>${L.length?L.map((r,k)=>{const s=calc(r).score;return`<div class="br"><span style="overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;white-space:nowrap">${ESC(r.name)}</span><div class="bt2"><i style="--w:${s}%;background:${MC[k%4]}"></i></div><b>${s}</b></div>`}).join(""):'<p class="mu">Your FinScores will appear here after your first analysis.</p>'}<a class="btn bl" href="#/comparemany" style="margin-top:8px">⚖️ Compare companies</a></div>`};
/* multi-company compare */
const CCOL=["#6366f1","#f59e0b","#10b981","#ec4899","#06b6d4","#8b5cf6"];
V.comparemany=()=>`${bar("Compare companies","home")}<div class="pg"><div class="card"><h2>Pick 2 to 6 reports</h2><p class="mu">Add more annual-report PDFs (or a sample company), then tick the ones to compare.</p><div id="cmlist"></div><button class="btn bl" data-act="cmup">📎 Add another PDF</button><button class="btn ol" data-act="cmsamp">🏢 Add a sample company</button></div><div id="cmres"></div></div>`;
function cmRender(){const l=$("#cmlist");if(!l)return;l.innerHTML=mine.length?mine.map(r=>`<label class="cmi"><input type="checkbox" data-cm="${r.id}" ${CM.includes(r.id)?"checked":""}><span><b>${ESC(r.name)}</b><small> · ${r.year} · ${calc(r).score}/100</small></span></label>`).join(""):'<p class="mu">No reports yet. Add a PDF or a sample company.</p>';
const S=CM.map(find).filter(Boolean);$("#cmres").innerHTML=S.length<2?`<div class="card es"><div class="em">⚖️</div><p class="mu">Select at least two reports to see the comparison dashboard.</p></div>`:cmDash(S);if(S.length>1)serverRank(S)}
function cmDash(S){const C=S.map(calc),n=S.length,rk=S.map((r,k)=>k).sort((a,b)=>C[b].score-C[a].score),ok=(k,j)=>C[k].M[j].status=="Valid"&&C[k].M[j].score!=null,
win=j=>{let b=-1,bs=-1;S.forEach((r,k)=>{if(ok(k,j)&&C[k].M[j].score>bs){bs=C[k].M[j].score;b=k}});return b},
lg=`<div class="lg">${S.map((r,k)=>`<span style="color:${CCOL[k]}">● ${ESC(r.name)}</span>`).join("")}</div>`,gw=300/4,bw=Math.min(22,(gw-10)/n);let g="";
["ROE","D/E","Cash","Growth"].forEach((t,j)=>{S.forEach((r,k)=>{const h=ok(k,j)?C[k].M[j].score:0;g+=`<rect class="gb" x="${j*gw+5+k*bw}" y="${115-h}" width="${bw-2}" height="${h}" rx="2" fill="${CCOL[k]}"/>`});g+=`<text x="${j*gw+gw/2}" y="131" font-size="9" text-anchor="middle" fill="currentColor">${t}</text>`});
const pr=[["profitability",0],["the lowest debt",1],["cash generation",2],["revenue growth",3]].map(([t,j])=>win(j)<0?null:`${S[win(j)].name} leads on ${t}`).filter(Boolean),
ins=`${S[rk[0]].name} has the highest FinScore, ${C[rk[0]].score} out of 100. ${pr.join(". ")}.`,tc=`grid-template-columns:70px repeat(${n},1fr)`,
row=(l,f,w)=>`<div class="tr2" style="${tc}"><span>${l}</span>${S.map((r,k)=>`<span class="${w==k?"win":""}">${f(k)}</span>`).join("")}</div>`;
return`<div class="card dsh"><h3>🏆 Ranking</h3>${rk.map((k,p)=>`<div class="br"><span style="overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;white-space:nowrap">${["🥇","🥈","🥉"][p]||(p+1)+"."} ${ESC(S[k].name)}</span><div class="bt2"><i style="--w:${C[k].score}%;background:${CCOL[k]}"></i></div><b>${C[k].score}</b></div>`).join("")}<button class="ch" style="margin:8px 0 0" data-say="${ESC(ins+" This is an analysis aid, not advice.")}">🔊 Listen</button></div>
<div class="card dsh"><h3>Metric by metric</h3>${lg}<svg viewBox="0 0 300 140" width="100%" role="img" aria-label="Grouped bar chart of metric scores">${g}<line x1="0" y1="115" x2="300" y2="115" stroke="var(--line)"/></svg></div>
<div class="card dsh" style="text-align:center"><h3>Strength radar</h3>${radar(S.map((r,k)=>({m:C[k].M.map((m,j)=>ok(k,j)?m.score:0),c:CCOL[k]})))}${lg}</div>
<div class="card dsh"><h3>Side by side</h3><div class="tr2" style="${tc}"><span></span>${S.map((r,k)=>`<span style="color:${CCOL[k]};font-weight:700">${ESC(r.name.split(" ")[0])}</span>`).join("")}</div>${row("FinScore",k=>C[k].score,rk[0])}${["ROE","D/E","Cash","Growth"].map((t,j)=>row(t,k=>C[k].M[j].disp,win(j))).join("")}<p class="mu" style="font-size:.85rem;margin:10px 0 0">${ESC(ins)} Illustrative only, not a recommendation.</p></div>`}
document.addEventListener("click",async e=>{const a=e.target.closest("[data-act=cmup],[data-act=cmsamp]");if(!a)return;if(a.dataset.act=="cmup"){cmM=true;nav("upload");return}const r=gen("annual-report-sample.pdf",2.4*1048576,true);mine=[r,...mine];await save(r);if(!CM.includes(r.id))CM.push(r.id);cmRender()});
document.addEventListener("change",e=>{const c=e.target.closest&&e.target.closest("[data-cm]");if(!c)return;const id=c.dataset.cm,k=CM.indexOf(id);if(c.checked){if(CM.length>=6){c.checked=false;toast("Compare up to 6 at a time");return}if(k<0)CM.push(id)}else if(k>-1)CM.splice(k,1);cmRender()});
addEventListener("hashchange",()=>{const h=location.hash.replace(/^#\/?/,"");if(h!=NAV){NAV=h;route()}});loadUser();route();boot();

/* ===== VOICE FIX: browsers block speech until the user taps once, so we unlock it + show a tap button + live subtitles ===== */
function showSub(el,t){let b=el.querySelector(".sub");if(!b){b=document.createElement("div");b.className="sub";el.appendChild(b)}b.textContent=t;b.hidden=!t}
function hideHint(){const h=$("#vhint");if(h)h.hidden=true}
function showHint(){let h=$("#vhint");if(!h){h=document.createElement("button");h.id="vhint";h.className="vhint";document.body.appendChild(h);h.onclick=()=>{RS.sound=true;SS.set("fs_snd","1");document.querySelectorAll("[data-ra=snd]").forEach(x=>x.textContent="🔊");speak(lastT,null,true);h.hidden=true}}
const none=!("speechSynthesis"in window)||!speechSynthesis.getVoices().length;h.textContent=none?"🔇 No voice on this browser. Try Chrome or Edge":"🔊 Tap to hear Fin";h.hidden=false}
function unlockVoice(){if(voiceOK||!("speechSynthesis"in window))return;try{const u=new SpeechSynthesisUtterance(" ");u.volume=0;speechSynthesis.speak(u);speechSynthesis.resume()}catch(e){}}
["pointerdown","keydown","touchstart"].forEach(ev=>document.addEventListener(ev,unlockVoice,{once:true,passive:true}));
document.addEventListener("visibilitychange",()=>{if(document.hidden){try{speechSynthesis.cancel()}catch(e){}}});
window.addEventListener("hashchange",()=>{if(!/reels/.test(location.hash))hideHint()});
